          <h2><strong>Solution with Open Source Software and Individual Theme Development</strong></h2>

          <p>The Open Mind Culture Shop goes along well visually with the blog website of the same name. It loads quickly, it is accessible, and it goes beyond the legal requirements thanks to the graphical visualization of price components. This builds trust, even among critical and ethically discerning customers. The online shop runs the free Community Edition and offers payments via Stripe and PayPal, both charging on a commission basis with no ongoing costs.</p>

          <p>Maintenance: The shop software can be updated by non-tech-savvy shop owners, at least in theory. Typically, this is handled either by the hosting providers for an additional fee, or by a certified Shopware developer like myself as part of a <a href="https://www.ingo-steinke.com/projects/legacy-migration-modernization-maintenance-case-study.html">maintenance contract</a>. That guarantees cost transparency, even regarding ongoing costs. Maintaining product data, such as prices, product descriptions, and images, is actually easy enough for non-experts to handle themselves, after a brief introduction and with existing products serving as templates. Training sessions, as well as interfaces for importing and synchronizing data between the online shop and an inventory management system, are also available upon request.</p>

          <h2><strong>Result: How Shopware pays off for small businesses as well</strong></h2>

          <p>I estimate the total effort up to operational readiness in the case presented at around 3 weeks (120 hours) of individual Shopware development. In individual cases, this varies significantly depending on the extent to which we can rely on existing templates or whether there are specific design requests. Therefore, I prepare a personalized proposal for each client following a no-obligation, complimentary initial consultation. Answering the question "how much does a website cost with you?" this case study now offers a reasonable figure.</p>

          <p>Monthly running costs remain in the double-digit range. There are also one-off costs estimated in the four-figure range for installation, theme development, and consulting. These figures demonstrate that it is possible to cost-effectively commission and operate a customized, accessible solution, even on the most affordable officially approved hosting.</p>

          <p>It should be noted that the test explicitly covered only a small shop with a limited number of products and orders. As economic success grows, demands, and consequently operating costs, typically increase as well. However, with the operating model described here, they do not grow to the same extent as is the case with some Software-as-a-Service providers. And thanks to open source software, every shop owner has the freedom to switch to another service provider at any time.</p>

          <p>By the way, anyone looking for a similarly transparent and cost-effective shop solution is welcome to get in touch with me.</p>

